 # Zipline MVP Partner-Confirmed Contract
@@ -37,6 +37,15 @@ freshness_reviewed: 2026-09-15
 
 Zipline answered the core partner questions for the Wonder 1P Drone Delivery MVP. A fulfillment-capable direct-order Quote requires valid mass and outer dimensions before Delivery Intent creation, while a separate mass-optional RDP discovery Quote is allowed for serviceability and KOETA timing features and is never consumed by Intent. An approved standard package within the confirmed limits is a single-Zip package; `DELIVERY_INTENT_STATUS_IN_PROGRESS` confirms successful loading and custody transfer; the exact planned customer drop-off point is not exposed; Dropbox loading summons the Drone; and `loading_window` is advisory rather than an expiration deadline. Zipline can also provision a separate non-production Partner Site, although the concrete access package is still pending.
 
+> [!warning] Owner edit 2026-11-02 — "and outer dimensions" (evidence pending)
+> On 2026-11-02 the vault owner edited the Short Answer above (git `6627297`, "Partner contract: dimensions also required") so that the fulfillment-capable Quote requires "valid mass **and outer dimensions**" before Delivery Intent. The edit is kept as the owner's statement, but it is not yet backed by a vault source and it diverges from the rest of this page and its neighbors:
+>
+> - The Confirmed Contract table below and [[zipline-mvp-final-partner-qa-working-draft-2026-07-26]] record the 2026-07-30 partner answer as a **mass** requirement only (`mass_grams`); no partner answer in the vault says a Quote needs dimensions.
+> - The Create Quote request carries `partner_site_id`, `prep_time_minutes`, `recipient`, and `mass_grams` and has no dimension fields; [[Questions for Zipline - Single-Delivery Guarantee and Multi-Delivery Handling (2026-07-15)]] states Create Quote "does not accept item dimensions". Dimension validation observed at runtime is on Pack, not Quote ([[zipline-sandbox-quote-mass-gating-contract]], [[zipline-discovery-vs-fulfillment-quote-mass-contract]]).
+> - What the vault *does* support is a **Wonder-side** precondition: the package must pass the full envelope (`2495 g`, `338 × 254 × 205 mm`, approved outer package) before Quote/Intent — see "Eligibility Service Impact" below and [[queries/1p-drone-delivery-eligibility-evaluation-trigger-and-revalidation-contract-2026-07-16|Eligibility Evaluation Trigger and Revalidation Contract]].
+>
+> Read the owner's sentence as that Wonder-side eligibility gate (mass and dimensions validated by Wonder before Intent), not as a new Zipline Quote API field. If Zipline has newly confirmed a dimension requirement on Quote, the source (date, channel) should be added to `sources` and the Confirmed Contract row updated; until then `freshness_status` is `watch`.
+
 > [!important] Source precedence
 > These 2026-07-30 partner answers supersede the assumption that a no-mass Quote can be used for direct-order fulfillment. Runtime validation and the confirmed Wonder RDP design refine the boundary: Create Quote accepts an omitted or `null` mass for non-binding discovery, but the resulting Quote must not be used for Delivery Intent. See [[zipline-discovery-vs-fulfillment-quote-mass-contract|Zipline Discovery vs Fulfillment Quote Mass Contract]].
 
